<title>BRAZIL: Two firms to set up sale of Brazil insurance shrs.</title>
<headline>Two firms to set up sale of Brazil insurance shrs.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium of Ernst &amp; Young Consultores and Banco Fator will design the sale of shares of Brazilian insurance firm Cia Uniao de Seguros Gerais, a unit of Rio Grande do Sul state's bank.</p>
<p>The state said in a statement that the group beat out three other bids and a contract will be signed next week giving Ernst &amp; Young and Banco Fator 120 days to conclude the work.</p>
<p>The stock sale is part of Rio Grande do Sul's state government reform program, which aims to draw private funds for infrastructure and co-management of state firms via the opening of capital stock to investors.</p>
<p>It did not say how large a stake of Union de Seguros Gerais would be sold or when. The insurer is a subsidiary of Banco do Estado do Rio Grande do Sul.</p>
<p>-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 232 4411</p>
